  "question": {
    "text": "A suitcase is gently dropped on a conveyor belt moving at a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the coefficient of friction between the belt and the suitcase is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, the displacement of the suitcase relative to conveyor belt before the slipping between the two is stopped, is (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
